From 12bfc9ecb7be0a48cd66f965b59ff38198d6943e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: licht <7687742+licht3345@user.noreply.gitee.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:09:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(p3): add chunked-synthesis example and env-gated
 semantic dump

P3 harness support, both additive and inert by default:

- examples/gpt_sovits_p3.rs: load the bundle once, then synthesize a supplied
  list of text chunks one at a time and concatenate them with the standard
  0.3 s fragment interval. Emits a per-chunk JSON report (chars, ms, samples,
  audio sec) plus total RTF, so P3 can measure per-chunk cost and map repeat
  events onto chunk boundaries. Equivalent chunking to the engine's own
  pre_seg_text contract (callers pass the already-split chunks).
- src/lib.rs: opt-in dump of the full pred_semantic token stream, written to
  $GSV_DUMP_SEMANTIC/semantic_tokens.jsonl. No behaviour change unless the
  env var is set (no I/O, no allocation on the default path).

Used to show the "repeat" is a VITS output-tail artefact rather than a
semantic loop-back: the repeated audio spans correspond to differing
semantic tokens (0/120 identical).
